From 3e0121f0eea22fcd8650d70e6b295e0a04a58bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:22:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soft renderer: memory asked for ahead (PLD), strips of 8 rows

es-mister-bench on the MiSTer: the ARM waits for each line of memory in
turn (a second core adds nothing), and asking for it ahead makes a faded
1080p layer 48.7 -> 28.1 ms, the copy to the screen 20.3 -> 16.3 ms, and
the carousel's whole frame 167 ms (strips of 16) -> 96.9 ms (strips of 8).

- every NEON span asks for its destination (PLDW) and its 1:1 source (PLD)
  256 bytes ahead; ES_SOFT_PLD (bytes, 0: none), PLD in es-mister.ini
- opaque pictures and scaled rows copied with copyPixels (NEON, PLD) in
  place of memcpy (26.6 -> 21.6 ms a frame on the MiSTer)
- the framebuffer copy asks for its source ahead
- ES_SOFT_STRIP and STRIP default to 8

PLD is a hint: the same pixels. ES_SOFT_DIRTY_CHECK on ARM (qemu): 0 of
368 frames different from the frame drawn whole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FcJn6v4DAFWH7rFwjpQQfk
